  "facts": {
    "patrol-known": "Corporal Haskett and Guardsman Wren are the only patrol on the King's Road this week, sent at the King's own wish to bring the Assembly's cushions in; the King asked to be told of anything on the road.",
    "wagons-crossed": "Garrow's ledger has twelve palace grain wagons crossing his bridge inward to the city this month, laden, though the city says palace wagons were lost to goblins."
  },
  "background": [
    "This is the same evening as the crossroads, a mile on along the King's Road. What happened at the crossroads is in what happened just before this scene, and that wins: how the fight there went, what the player found on the goblins, and how Fitch and Tansy stand with them. Fitch and Tansy are coming on behind with the cart, and arrive once the bridge is clear."
  ],
  "reinforcements": [
    {
      "id": "axemen",
      "name": "two Kläggenheim axemen",
      "statblock": "tough",
      "weapon": "greataxe",
      "look": "Two vast Kläggenheim axemen in fur and iron, beards in plaits, riding shaggy northern ponies far too small for them and roaring the same word over and over (it means 'breakfast').",
      "after": 3,
      "why": "The Kläggenheim delegation's baggage guard, riding a mile behind on the road with their delegation's luggage for the Assembly, come up at the gallop at the horn and the noise, axes out and roaring."
    }
